      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the 1960s the city earned the nickname Brazil's Automobile Capital after German and American automakers built factories there.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%A3o_Bernardo_do_Campo",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Central Única dos Trabalhadores, Latin America's largest trade union, was founded in São Bernardo do Campo.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/S%C3%A3o_Bernardo_do_Campo",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Vera Cruz Film Studios, which launched many Brazilian actors in the 1950s and 1960s, once stood in the city.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%A3o_Bernardo_do_Campo",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The city hosts the Children's City amusement park, built on the former Vera Cruz studio lot.",
